---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', name: `About ${SITE.name}`,
  mainEntity: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.author.name, url: `${SITE.url}/about/`, sameAs: ['https://www.imdb.com/name/nm2420157/'], jobTitle: 'Learning designer and filmmaker' },
}];
---
<Page
  title="About"
  description="The Learning Curve is an independent publication on how to design online courses that work, founded by learning designer and filmmaker Jim Lounsbury."
  standfirst="An independent publication on how to design online courses that work."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>
    Most advice about building online courses is written to sell you a platform. Most research on how people learn is
    written for other researchers. The Learning Curve sits between the two: it reads the research, explains what it
    means for a real course, and judges the platforms on how well they help people learn.
  </p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The Library:</strong> one evergreen page per learning principle, each re-checked against new research every year.</li>
    <li><strong>Guides:</strong> practical course design and instructional design, grounded in the evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Reviews:</strong> course platforms scored with <a href="/how-we-review/">one published method</a>, from hands-on testing.</li>
    <li><strong>Trends:</strong> dated news on where online education is going, and what it means for people who build courses.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
  <p>
    The Learning Curve was founded by Jim Lounsbury, a learning designer and documentary filmmaker based in Sydney.
    Jim works in educational development at Avondale University, designing course content and microcredentials, and
    runs CredentialCraft, a course-design studio. Alongside that, he has spent his career making
    documentaries and factual television in more than 20 countries, and his work can be seen on Apple TV, Prime
    Video, Stan, National Geographic and more.
  </p>
  <p>
    That mix shapes the publication: a learning designer's respect for evidence, and a filmmaker's sense of what
    keeps people watching.
  </p>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    We use AI tools to help research and draft articles. Every article is reviewed, edited and approved by Jim before
    it is published, every research claim links to its source, and every platform claim is checked in the platform
    itself. Documentary-style photographs on this site are AI-generated illustrations.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site earns money through affiliate links, which never decide what we cover or how we score it. The
    <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a> has the details.
  </p>
  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Corrections, research we should read, or a platform we should test: <a href="mailto:hello@thelearningcurve.net">hello@thelearningcurve.net</a>.</p>
</Page>
